[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-0f497b0c-05dd-4241-87db-e95f95b39d34\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Wed 14 Oct 2026 11:00 - 11:15 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2026/ase-2026-venue1-forum-2\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Forum 2</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Testing and Analysis: Automated Program Repair and Synthesis 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/junjiewang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Junjie Wang</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"0f497b0c-05dd-4241-87db-e95f95b39d34\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>MultiFixer: A Coordinator-Proposer Based Multi-agent Framework for Fixing Multi-hunk Bugs</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Automated Program Repair (APR) has benefited greatly from Large Language Models (LLMs), but existing LLM-based APR methods still struggle with multi-hunk bugs that require coordinated changes across multiple locations. These bugs demand repository-level context understanding, repair-order scheduling, and effective hunk-level patch generation and selection. To address these challenges, we propose MultiFixer, a novel Coordinator-Proposer based multi-agent framework for multi-hunk repair.<br>\nMultiFixer performs tool-augmented bug analysis, constructs fine-grained repair context, iteratively generates patches through a Coordinator-Proposer architecture, and applies two-stage patch refinement for syntactic and semantic correctness. We evaluate MultiFixer on 835 bugs from Defects4J and three vulnerability benchmarks. On Defects4J, MultiFixer fixes 326 bugs, including 62 multi-method and 27 multi-file bugs, and outperforms prior APR baselines in the reported comparisons with the same base model. Moreover, MultiFixer also fixes 46 multi-hunk bugs among 95 unique fixes. When combined with Claude-3.5-Sonnet, MultiFixer repairs 420 bugs, establishing a new state of the art on Defects4J. On VUL4J, MultiFixer repairs 24 real-world vulnerabilities, including 5 multi-hunk cases. On the multi-hunk subsets of SEC-bench and PatchEval, MultiFixer fixes 11 and 19 vulnerabilities, respectively, outperforming all compared baselines under GPT-3.5. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of MultiFixer for multi-hunk repair.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837527\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/haichuanhu2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">hai <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>chuan hu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University of Science and Technology</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/chunrongfang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Chunrong Fang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage